design:
Pipeline: recaps -> extractCampaignBible -> bible; then composeArcSummary(recaps, bible) -> summary; then single rollupArcSummary(summary, bible) DB write.

NEW packages/core/src/memory/campaignBibleExtractor.ts:
  extractCampaignBible(model: ModelClient, input: {
    campaignId: string;
    recaps: SessionRecapRecord[];
  }): Promise<CampaignBibleInput>

Pure read-side (no DB). System prompt asks the model to emit a dedicated fenced JSON block (following the existing parseToolCalls pattern in orchestrator/protocol.ts — fence tag 'bible_json'). Internal: regex-match the fence -> JSON.parse -> shape-check (object with worldFacts/majorNpcs/factions/openThreads each a string[]) -> return CampaignBibleInput. Throws MemorySummaryError on missing-fence / unparseable / wrong-shape. ModelClientError from the provider propagates.

MOD packages/core/src/memory/arcSummary.ts:
  composeArcSummary signature gains `bible: CampaignBibleInput`. The user message gets a bible-rendered prelude (4 buckets, one section each). System prompt gains a line telling the model to reference the bible's NPCs/factions canonically.

CLI orchestration in packages/cli/src/play.ts:

  async function rollupCampaignArc(deps, db, campaignId) {
    const recaps = ...; if (recaps.length === 0) return;
    let bible;
    try { bible = await extractBibleWithRetry(deps.model, { campaignId, recaps }); }
    catch (e) { deps.io.write('Arc rollup skipped (bible extraction failed): ' + msg + '.'); return; }
    let summary;
    try { summary = await composeArcSummary(deps.model, { campaignId, arcId: CAMPAIGN_ARC_ID, recaps, bible }); }
    catch (e) { deps.io.write('Arc rollup skipped (arc summary failed): ' + msg + '.'); return; }
    rollupArcSummary(db, { campaignId, arcId: CAMPAIGN_ARC_ID, summary, sourceSessionIds, campaignBible: bible, createdAt: deps.now() });
  }

  async function extractBibleWithRetry(model, input) {
    try { return await extractCampaignBible(model, input); }
    catch { return await extractCampaignBible(model, input); }  // one retry; if this throws, propagate
  }

extractBibleWithRetry is a private CLI helper (policy lives in CLI; core stays pure).

Error handling:
  - Bible fails once -> silent retry
  - Bible fails twice -> warning 'bible extraction failed' + atomic skip; no DB write
  - Bible succeeds, summary fails -> warning 'arc summary failed' + atomic skip; no DB write
  - Both succeed -> single rollupArcSummary write

Single DB write at the tail means partial state never lands.

